/-
# Dynamic local spin-ray/off-ray family on the common completed path

The viable finite route supplies, at each physical scale, a cofinal spin-ray
capacity and a cofinal off-ray residual coercivity.  The fixed-nome compiler
turns those data into the actual completed canonical vacuum-sector transfer.
This module performs that construction scale by scale and then forgets only
the finite proof route into the source-independent dynamic completed-family
interface.

The exact strength of the resulting transfer is

  ((1/2) * rayCapacity.delta) * uniformSectorMassFloor,

and the completed rate is definitionally `1 / (1 + strength)`.  The module
therefore supplies the normalized-strength law needed by the common physical
rate compiler while retaining the literal same-object completed moments.

No dynamic residual family, strength/spacing band, graph-norm limit,
continuum measure, continuum Yang--Mills theory, or Clay conclusion is
inhabited here.  No `Classical.*`, choice, `native_decide`, `sorry`, custom
axiom, or noncomputable declaration is used.
-/

import YMGap.Continuum.BF4PhysicalDynamicVacuumSectorCompletedFamily
